Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Quantum Machine Learning in Phase Space", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A quantum circuit is a tensor network, and a tensor network contraction is \
a sequence of array products - the computation a neural net performs. The \
framework closes that loop: a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumCircuitOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 " compiles to a tensor network, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Wolfram`TensorNetworks`", "InlineCode"]], "InlineCode",
  ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 " contracts that network into a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NetGraph"]], "paclet:ref/NetGraph"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " rather than an array, with every circuit tensor held in a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NetArrayLayer"]], "paclet:ref/NetArrayLayer"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 ". The circuit becomes the model. Nothing about the forward computation is \
assembled by hand; the only layer added here is the loss."
}], "Text",
 CellID->329621944,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
The net framework computes over real numbers, and that is not an obstacle: in \
the phase-space picture a state is a Wigner quasi-probability vector and \
every circuit tensor is real, so the whole pipeline stays inside what a net \
can represent. This tutorial compiles a circuit to a net, differentiates \
through it, and trains a gate until gradient descent recovers a rotation \
angle.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->515379898,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<<", " ", "Wolfram`QuantumFramework`"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->604760901,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["A Circuit Is the Model", "Section",
 CellID->1476799103,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell["\<\
A circuit can carry its own initial state, so the whole computation - \
prepare, then rotate - is one object:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->448336599,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qc", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<RY\>\"", "[", "0.7", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->970785311,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell["Its diagram shows the state feeding the gate:", "Text",
 CellID->1377816002,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qc", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1439899046,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumPhaseSpaceTransform"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " moves it to the phase-space picture, where each qubit's 2-dimensional \
Hilbert space becomes a 4-dimensional space of Wigner components:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1641200340,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ps", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumPhaseSpaceTransform", "[", "qc", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1424533854,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell["The Circuit as a Tensor Network", "Section",
 CellID->535457321,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<TensorNetwork\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " property compiles the circuit into a network of one tensor per element. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Computational\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " keeps the tensors in the phase-space frame, where they are real; without \
it, basis-change tensors in the computational frame enter and are complex:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->141959522,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tn", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ps", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<TensorNetwork\>\"", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Computational\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->299517738,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell["\<\
The largest imaginary part across every entry of every tensor is exactly zero:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2142391071,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Im", "[", 
       RowBox[{"N", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Normal", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}],
     " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TensorNetworkTensors", "[", "tn", "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1002769646,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell["\<\
The network is a graph, with the state and the gate as its two nodes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->436346740,ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ps", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\"\<TensorNetworkGraph\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Computational\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->2122865143,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell["Contracting to a Net", "Section",
 CellID->1735808809,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Wolfram`TensorNetworks`", "InlineCode"]], "InlineCode",
  ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " chooses the pairwise contraction order:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->753514147,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"path", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"GreedyContractionPath", "[", "tn", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1164297175,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["TensorNetworkContraction"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<NetGraph\>\""}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 " performs the same contraction, but instead of computing the array it wires \
the computation as a net: each leaf tensor becomes a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NetArrayLayer"]], "paclet:ref/NetArrayLayer"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 ", and each pairwise contraction becomes reshape, transpose and dot layers:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->632614636,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"net", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"TensorNetworkContraction", "[", 
   RowBox[{"tn", ",", " ", "path", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<NetGraph\>\""}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->1689610856,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell["\<\
The net takes no input and its output is the state the circuit produces, so \
running it gives the Wigner vector directly - no separate state extraction:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1303163127,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"net", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->2098230307,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell["\<\
That is the Wigner vector of the state an RY rotation by 0.7 produces from \
the initial one:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1930159659,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"N", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumPhaseSpaceTransform", "[", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "0.35", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "0.35", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
     "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1113655915,ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell["\<\
Because the net is a source net, it is also an array container: its shape \
reads off the output port with nothing evaluated:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1606118752,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ArrayDimensions", "[", "net", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->2141499446,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell["The Gate as a Trainable Parameter", "Section",
 CellID->339082558,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To train a gate rather than a state, compile the gate alone. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<PrependInitial\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " no initial state is attached, and the net's output is the gate's own \
phase-space kernel:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->432388834,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"gate", "[", "theta_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"QuantumPhaseSpaceTransform", "[", 
         RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<RY\>\"", "[", "theta", "]"}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",",
        " ", "t"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"t", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"p", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<TensorNetwork\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Computational\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<PrependInitial\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"TensorNetworkContraction", "[", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"GreedyContractionPath", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<NetGraph\>\""}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gate", "[", "0.7", "]"}], "[", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->443736588,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell["\<\
The kernel is a rotation by the angle in its middle block, so the angle can \
be read straight off it:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1593449978,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ArcTan", " ", "@@", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gate", "[", "0.7", "]"}], "[", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1742646261,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell["Learning the Angle", "Section",
 CellID->29467524,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take the circuit at 0.7 as the target and a circuit at 0 as the model. The \
only thing built by hand is the loss: the compiled circuit becomes one node \
of a net whose other node is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["MeanAbsoluteLossLayer"]], "paclet:ref/MeanAbsoluteLossLayer"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1939141443,ExpressionUUID->"5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"target", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"gate", "[", "0.7", "]"}], "[", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"lossNet", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"NetGraph", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<circuit\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gate", "[", "0.", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<loss\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"MeanAbsoluteLossLayer", "[", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}], ",", "\n", 
    "    ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<circuit\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"NetPort", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<loss\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Input\>\""}], "]"}]}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"NetPort", "[", "\"\<Target\>\"", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"NetPort", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<loss\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Target\>\""}], "]"}]}]}], 
     "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->5047578,ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell["\<\
Compiling the circuit made the gate a learnable parameter of the net. It is \
the only one:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->15008895,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Keys", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Information", "[", 
   RowBox[{"lossNet", ",", " ", "\"\<Arrays\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1892712309,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The target enters through an input port, and the loss comes out of an \
output port, which is all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NetTrain"]], "paclet:ref/NetTrain"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 " needs:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->787969749,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Information", "[", 
  RowBox[{"lossNet", ",", " ", "\"\<InputPorts\>\""}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->525088789,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell["The model starts at the identity, an angle of zero:", "Text",
 CellID->357930410,ExpressionUUID->"337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ArcTan", " ", "@@", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"NetExtract", "[", 
      RowBox[{"lossNet", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<circuit\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<tensor\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Array\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->1802489801,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"lossNet", "[", 
  RowBox[{"<|", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Target\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "target"}], "|>"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->115301326,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Training is then ordinary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NetTrain"]], "paclet:ref/NetTrain"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 ": one example, the net's own ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Loss\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 " port as the objective, and the gate array is what gets updated."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1651187567,ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"trained", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NetTrain", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lossNet", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Target\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "target", "}"}]}], "|>"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"LossFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Loss\>\""}], ",", "\n", 
     "    ", 
     RowBox[{"MaxTrainingRounds", " ", "->", " ", "2000"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"TrainingProgressReporting", " ", "->", " ", "None"}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"trained", "[", 
  RowBox[{"<|", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Target\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "target"}], "|>"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->941376513,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell["\<\
Training through the compiled circuit recovered the rotation angle:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2120243592,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ArcTan", " ", "@@", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"NetExtract", "[", 
      RowBox[{"trained", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<circuit\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<tensor\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Array\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->1047559317,ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell["Details", "Section",
 CellID->1820947576,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<NetGraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 " is a valid ",
 Cell[BoxData["Method"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " value for ",
 Cell[BoxData["TensorNetworkContraction"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " but is deliberately absent from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Wolfram`TensorNetworks`$TensorNetworkContractionMethods", 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 ", which lists the interchangeable methods that all return arrays."
}], "Item",
 CellID->670734585,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A compiled circuit is a source net: no input ports, and an output port \
carrying the shape. That is what makes it an array container in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Wolfram`Arrays`", "InlineCode"]], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " sense, and what lets it be a node inside a larger net."
}], "Item",
 CellID->58232708,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The gate array sits at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<tensor\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Array\>\""}], "}"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 " in a gate-only circuit; a multi-tensor circuit names its leaves ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<tensor1\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<tensor2\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " and so on, which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"NetExtract", "[", 
   RowBox[{"net", ",", " ", "All"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " lists."
}], "Item",
 CellID->393464600,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell["Possible Issues", "Section",
 CellID->1484396876,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Without ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Computational\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 " the compiled tensors carry basis-change factors from the computational \
frame and are complex, and complex arrays cannot be lifted into net layers, \
so the contraction names the offending tensor and fails:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1149283354,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tnComputational", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ps", "[", "\"\<TensorNetwork\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"TensorNetworkContraction", "[", 
  RowBox[{"tnComputational", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GreedyContractionPath", "[", "tnComputational", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<NetGraph\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1092188694,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A contraction path belongs to the network it was derived from. That network \
has five tensors where the phase-space one has two, so reusing the earlier ",
 Cell[BoxData["path"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 " reports the arity mismatch before it ever reaches the complex tensors:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->559599970,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TensorNetworkContraction", "[", 
  RowBox[{"tnComputational", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<NetGraph\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->1710123944,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NetTrain"]], "paclet:ref/NetTrain"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 " reports a final loss rather than an exact zero, so these are converged \
numbers rather than a closed form. The individual entries of the trained \
kernel are not stable between runs - they drift along a scaling that leaves \
their ratio fixed - while the angle read from that ratio is, which is why the \
angle is what the example reports."
}], "Text",
 CellID->934597701,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell["\<\
Training a gate against a single input state does not determine it. The gate \
above is trained against its whole kernel, which pins every column; fitting \
only the circuit's output vector would leave the gate's action on the rest of \
the space free, and the recovered angle would mean nothing.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->284780108,ExpressionUUID->"6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],

